{"name":"True V","hex":"#8e72c7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"true","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Conforming to the actual state of reality or fact; factually correct.","As an ellipsis of \"(while) it is true (that)\", used to start a sentence"]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Accurately; in alignment.","Truthfully."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/true"}],"entries":[{"title":"V","blocks":[{"text":"V is the twenty-second letter of the Latin alphabet, used in the modern English alphabet, the alphabets of other western European languages and others worldwide. Its name in English is vee, plural vees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Latin_letter_V.svg/330px-Latin_letter_V.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V","wikidata":"Q9963"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Newes_ABC_Buchlein_MET_DP855605.jpg/500px-Newes_ABC_Buchlein_MET_DP855605.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Newes_ABC_Buchlein_MET_DP855605.jpg/1280px-Newes_ABC_Buchlein_MET_DP855605.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Newes_ABC_Buchlein_MET_DP855605.jpg/500px-Newes_ABC_Buchlein_MET_DP855605.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Late Renaissance or early Baroque design of ⟨v⟩, from 1627","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANewes_ABC_Buchlein_MET_DP855605.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Corinthian_Vase_depicting_Perseus%2C_Andromeda_and_Ketos.jpg/500px-Corinthian_Vase_depicting_Perseus%2C_Andromeda_and_Ketos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: